  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9027734d34a03bb43947e2332bd51243, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Dear owner,


    Malai again. I hear your mango sticky rice makes
    people smile. Good. Now something with a little fire.


    Tom yum was my father''s
    cure for everything. A cold, a bad day, a broken heart. He would stand over the
    pot and say, "If your nose doesn''t run, it isn''t tom yum."


    Lemongrass
    bruised so it gives everything, lime added at the very end, and shrimp that only
    just turn pink. Never let them boil too long.


    Sour, spicy, salty, a little
    sweet. Life is never only one taste.'
